@nsobid-FF1D1C05670DB6021C85B624A710B963

# Animal Crossing: New Horizons 3.0.3 - Double Buffering

@flag print_values
@flag offset_shift 0x100

// Forces a two-texture swapchain.
//
// The sead::GameFrameworkNx here switches the NVN window between 2 and 3
// active textures at runtime. It starts from CreateArg isTripleBuffer
// (framework +0xBD), the present path raises the count to 3 whenever a
// frame takes longer than the framework's threshold and drops back to 2
// once frames are short again, and a pending request byte (+0x245) can
// force either count. Every route to 3 is closed here, so the CPU can run
// at most one frame ahead of scanout.

@enabled
// initial buffer count: isTripleBuffer read as false
037B84A4 09008052   // MOV W9,#0 (was LDRB W9,[X19,#0xBD])
// slow-frame auto switch from 2 to 3 never fires
037B9834 13000014   // B to the present call (was B.LE)
// a triple-buffer request (1) selects 2, like the double-buffer request (0)
037B9850 3F090071   // CMP W9,#2 (was CMP W9,#3)
037B9858 41008052   // MOV W1,#2 (was MOV W1,#3)
@stop

// Offsets reverse-engineered against Animal Crossing: New Horizons 3.0.3
// (sead + agl/gsys, NVN). The retail build is symbol-stripped; every site was
// located by structure and byte-verified against the IDB before being written.
//
// https://github.com/RAMDRAGONS/switch-patches
